<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mrs. Joliot-Curie returns two days after her first visit and was seen this morning by Dr. Engquist-Mensah of hematology/oncology, who performed a bone marrow aspiration and biopsy. She feels more tired than two days ago and is breathless on one flight of stairs. Her gums still ooze when she brushes, and two new bruises have appeared on her thighs. She has had no fever, chills, nosebleeds, blood in the urine or stool, headache, or confusion. She has avoided aspirin as advised. She has written down her history of radiation work and the laboratory accident, and has begun asking her employer&apos;s radiation safety office for her dose records. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Symptoms</td><td>More tired; breathless on one flight; gum oozing; new bruises; no fever</td></tr><tr><td>Weight</td><td>53.8 kg</td></tr><tr><td>Testing today</td><td>Bone marrow aspiration and biopsy with flow cytometry, cytogenetics and molecular panel; blood count; INR and fibrinogen; hepatitis B, hepatitis C and HIV tests; HLA typing; chest X-ray</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

